{
  "Name": "Okta - Threats & Platform - Possible Okta DoS Attack",
  "Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Threats & Platform\nMITRE ATT&CK: Impact / T1498\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Possible Okta DoS Attack\" or \"<ip>|Possible Okta DoS Attack\"\n\nDetects Okta rate-limit and concurrency-limit violations: system.operation.rate_limit.violation, system.client.rate_limit.violation, system.client.concurrency_rate_limit.violation (the event types Okta emits today) plus the older system.org.rate_limit.*, application.integration.rate_limit_exceeded and core.concurrency.org.limit.violation. Sustained violations can indicate a denial-of-service attempt or an integration abusing the API. Risk floor Medium (55).\n\nFalse positives: misbehaving or bursty integrations and scripts. Tune with okta_ip_allowlist.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/impact_possible_okta_dos_attack/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/impact_possible_okta_dos_attack.toml",
